hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21597","Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, or from a man of the Ansar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever recites by saying: He is Allah, the One, it is as if he recited a third of the Qur'an."
"21598","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, and Abdullah said: And Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to me, Khalid al-Wasiti informed us. Al-Thaqafi said in his hadith: Abu Mas'ud al-Jurayri narrated to us. Wahb said: Khalid informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: Prayer in a single garment is sunnah. We used to do it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was not blamed upon us. Ibn Mas'ud said: That was only when there was fewness in clothes. As for when Allah has widened, prayer in two garments is purer."
"21599","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Hasan ibn Musa and 'Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, and 'Affan said: Thabit informed us, from Abu Rafi', from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abdullah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seclude in the last ten of Ramadan. He traveled one year and did not seclude. When the next year came, he secluded twenty days."
"21600","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Hasan ibn Musa and 'Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, and 'Affan said: Thabit informed us, from Abu Rafi', from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abdullah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seclude in the last ten of Ramadan. He traveled one year and did not seclude. When the next year came, he secluded twenty days."
"21601","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Ubayy, and Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to me, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from some of his companions, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Ubayy, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked him which verse in the Book of Allah is greatest. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He repeated it several times, then Ubayy said: Ayat al-Kursi. He said: May knowledge please you, Abu al-Mundhir. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it has a tongue and two lips sanctifying the King at the leg of the Throne. And this is the wording of the hadith of Ubayy from Abd al-Razzaq."
"21602","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Ubayy, and Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to me, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from some of his companions, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Ubayy, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked him which verse in the Book of Allah is greatest. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He repeated it several times, then Ubayy said: Ayat al-Kursi. He said: May knowledge please you, Abu al-Mundhir. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it has a tongue and two lips sanctifying the King at the leg of the Throne. And this is the wording of the hadith of Ubayy from Abd al-Razzaq."
"21603","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah, from Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me as a zakat collector over Bali and Udhrah and all Banu Sad and Hudhaym ibn Qudaah. My father said, and Yaqub said in another place, from Qudaah. He said: So I collected their zakat until I passed by the last man among them, and his dwelling and land were the nearest of their dwellings to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Madinah. He said: When he gathered his property to me, I found due on it only a bint makhad, meaning a one-year-old she-camel, so I informed him that it was his zakat. He said: That is what has no milk in it and no back to ride, and by Allah, neither the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor any messenger of his ever stood over my property before you, and I would not lend to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, from my property what has no milk in it and no back, but this is a young fat she-camel, so take it. He said: So I said to him: I will not take what I was not commanded to take, and this Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is near to you, so if you wish to come to him and offer to him what you offered to me, do so; if he accepts it from you he accepts it, and if he rejects it for you he rejects it. He said: I will do so. He said: So he went out with me, bringing the she-camel he had offered me, until we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he said to him: O Prophet of Allah, your messenger came to me to take the zakat of my property, and by Allah, neither the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor any messenger of his ever stood over my property before him, so I gathered my property for him and he claimed that due on me is a bint makhad, and that is what has no milk in it and no back, and I offered him a young fat she-camel of mine for him to take, but he refused me that, and here she is, I have come to you with her, O Messenger of Allah, take her. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: That which is due on you is that, but if you volunteer good we will accept it from you and Allah will reward you for it. He said: So here she is, O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you with her, take her. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered it to be taken and supplicated for blessing for him in his property."
"21604","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Yahya ibn Abdullah, from Umarah ibn Hazm, Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him as a zakat collector, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ubayy, and he added in it: Umarah said: I was put in charge of their zakats in the time of Muawiyah, and I took from that man thirty hiqqahs for one thousand five hundred camels due on him."
"21605","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, al-Khuzai said in his hadith: Ubayy ibn Kab said, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led the people in prayer and omitted a verse, then said: Which of you caught anything of my recitation for me. So Ubayy said: I did, O Messenger of Allah, you omitted such-and-such verse. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I knew, if anyone would catch it for me, it is you."
"21606","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, al-Khuzai said in his hadith: Ubayy ibn Kab said, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led the people in prayer and omitted a verse, then said: Which of you caught anything of my recitation for me. So Ubayy said: I did, O Messenger of Allah, you omitted such-and-such verse. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I knew, if anyone would catch it for me, it is you."
"21607","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from one who narrated to him, from the umm walad of Ubayy ibn Kab, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that a man entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: When was your last encounter with Umm Mildam, and it is heat between the skin and the flesh. He said: That is a pain that never afflicted me at all. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The likeness of the believer is like the young plant, turning red once and turning yellow another time."
"21608","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, intended to forbid tamattu in Hajj, so Ubayy said to him: That is not yours, we performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not forbid us that, so Umar turned away from that. And he intended to forbid robes of hibarah because they are dyed with urine, so Ubayy said to him: That is not yours, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wore them, and we wore them in his time."
"21609","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sasaa ibn Sawhan, he said: He came with a group with him and they found a whip, so its owner took it, and they neither commanded him nor forbade him. So I came to Madinah and Ubayy ibn Kab met us, so we asked him, and he said: I found one hundred dinars in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Announce it for a year. He repeated it to him until he mentioned three years. So I said: O Messenger of Allah. So he said: It is yours."
"21610","Abdullah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Said al-Ruqashi al-Khazzaz narrated to me, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Ibn al-Fadl, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, put between your adhan and your iqamah a breath in which the eater finishes his food at leisure and the one performing ablution relieves his need at leisure."
"21611","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzaz narrated to me, Qurrah ibn Habib informed us, Muarik ibn Abbad al-Abdi informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Fadl informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jawza, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, and he mentioned the like of it."
"21612","Abdullah narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Numayr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited Baraah on Friday while standing, reminding of the days of Allah, with Ubayy ibn Kab facing the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu al-Darda and Abu Dharr. Then one of them nudged Ubayy ibn Kab and said: When was this surah revealed, O Ubayy, for I did not hear it except now. So he gestured to him to be silent. When they finished, he said: I asked you when this surah was revealed and you did not inform me. Ubayy said: You have nothing of your prayer today except what you engaged in idly. So I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him and informed him of what Ubayy said, and he said: Ubayy spoke the truth."
"21613","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Musayyabi narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, he said: Ibn Shihab said, Anas ibn Malik said: Abu Dharr used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah, then Jibril, peace be upon him, descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water, then came with a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith and emptied it into my chest, then closed it, then took my hand and ascended with me to heaven. When he came to the lowest heaven he sought opening, and it was said: Who is this. He said: Jibril. It was said: Is anyone with you. He said: Yes, Muhammad is with me. It was said: Was he sent for. He said: Yes, so open. When we rose over the lowest heaven, there was a man with black forms on his right and black forms on his left, and when he looked toward his right he smiled, and when he looked toward his left he wept. He said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. He said: I said to Jibril, peace be upon him: Who is this. He said: This is Adam, and these black forms on his right and left are the souls of his children; the people of the right are the people of Paradise, and the black forms on his left are the people of the Fire; when he looks toward his right he laughs, and when he looks toward his left he weeps. He said: Then Jibril, peace be upon him, ascended with me until he came to the second heaven and said to its keeper: Open. Its keeper said to him like what the keeper of the lowest heaven said, and he opened for him. Anas ibn Malik said: He mentioned that he found in the heavens Adam and Idris and Musa and Isa and Ibrahim, peace and blessings be upon them, but he did not establish for me how their stations were, except that he mentioned that he found Adam in the lowest heaven and Ibrahim in the sixth heaven. Anas said: When Jibril, peace be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by Idris, he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. He said: So I said: Who is this. He said: This is Idris. He said: Then I passed by Musa and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this. He said: This is Musa. Then I passed by Isa and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this. He said: This is Isa ibn Maryam. He said: Then I passed by Ibrahim and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. I said: Who is this. He said: This is Ibrahim, peace be upon him. Ibn Shihab said: And Ibn Hazm informed me that Ibn Abbas and Abu Habbah al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then I was ascended until I appeared at a level where I heard the scratching of the pens. Ibn Hazm and Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, obligated upon my ummah fifty prayers. He said: So I returned with that until I passed by Musa, peace be upon him, and he said: What did your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, obligate upon your ummah. I said: He obligated upon them fifty prayers. So Musa, peace be upon him, said to me: Return to your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, for your ummah cannot bear that. He said: So I returned to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He reduced half of it. So I returned to Musa and informed him, and he said: Return to your Lord, for your ummah cannot bear that. He said: So I returned to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He said: They are five and they are fifty, the word is not changed with Me. He said: So I returned to Musa, peace be upon him, and he said: Return to your Lord. So I said: I am too shy before my Lord, Blessed and Exalted. He said: Then he went with me until he brought me to Sidrat al-Muntaha. He said: It was covered by colors I do not know what they are. He said: Then I was entered into Paradise, and in it were domes of pearl, and its soil was musk. This is the end of the musnad of Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah Exalted be pleased with him."
